  "limitations": "Eight conditional60 judgments and total60; not an objective full-FUA measurement or global ranking. GSS now incorporates local outcomes/protection and root correction of a missed88%non-repeat claim. Sample/window/control/gang classification are unknown. Impact/group/FUA, ordinary reach, continuity and timing bridges are necessary and revocable; withdrawal of GSS gives51–66 without a centre. Other seven judgments unchanged, including their own LON net payment/monitoring and RES access assumptions. No supported exclusion or qualified32nd threshold.",
  "dimensions": [
    {
      "id": "PCS",
      "score": 60,
      "rationale": "Actual cooling/water places and stormwater/road maintenance support protection; heat-island exposure, heavy rain and winter hazards remain material. Carbon targets are not protection outcomes.",
      "assumption": "Reviewed cooling and maintenance usually work and reach ordinary residents; city-core evidence reasonably represents FUA397 and persists to cutoff. Unreviewed geophysical scenarios are not treated as absent.",
      "conditionalAlternatives": [40, 80],
      "subpillars": {
        "heat_humidity": "partial",
        "flood_sea_level": "partial",
        "geophysical": "context",
        "severe_weather_wildfire": "partial"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "GSS",
      "score": 60,
      "rationale": "Local reported emerging youth gangs and persistent safety concerns remain. Resident safety observations, actual Ankkuri interventions with a reported 88% non-repeat claim, neighbourhood improvement/continuation, local participation in completed VESKY protection and actual PAPU coordination jointly support limited usual impact and real mitigation. The 88% lacks denominator/window/control/gang classification; neither it nor safety feelings measure citywide organised-violence harm.",
      "assumption": "Accept limited city/provider-to-FUA397 and targeted-youth-to-usual-resident applicability; post-help coercion is important for some groups but does not generally block necessary ordinary activities. Actual interventions/shared utility protection remain usually reachable and continue to cutoff; dated versions/2025 observations remain applicable. These are revocable judgments, not measured all-population effects. Refusing a necessary impact/scope/continuity/timing bridge restores null and empty alternatives. Evidence of material residual necessary-activity constraints can support40 without any majority-victim requirement; stronger low residuals may support80.",
      "conditionalAlternatives": [40, 80],
      "subpillars": {
        "organized_violence": "partial",
        "regional_conflict": "context",
        "strategic_exposure": "partial"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ISR",
      "score": 60,
      "rationale": "Completed service/transport changes, actual handling of cyber events and food assistance demonstrate execution; fiscal/staff pressure and unmet assistance persist after mitigation. Plans and exercises do not prove all-crisis recovery.",
      "assumption": "Observed execution remains representative of major ordinary services in FUA397; known coordination and fiscal constraints remain material but do not generally prevent necessary service. Crisis-specific reach is not measured.",
      "conditionalAlternatives": [40, 80],
      "subpillars": {
        "governance": "partial",
        "adaptive_capacity": "partial",
        "social_cohesion": "partial",
        "emergency_recovery": "partial"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "RES",
      "score": 60,
      "rationale": "Actual municipal water service, energy production/storage and food distribution support usual supply; unmet food requests and cost pressure remain important counterevidence. Regional delivery does not measure every household.",
      "assumption": "Water/energy service and ordinary market food are usually available and affordable for a median-income citizen. Food-aid rationing is serious but is not assumed to represent all median-income residents; service-area and continuity assumptions remain explicit.",
      "conditionalAlternatives": [40, 80],
      "subpillars": {
        "water": "partial",
        "food": "partial",
        "energy": "partial",
        "supply_chain": "partial"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "MED",
      "score": 60,
      "rationale": "2025 actual primary and specialist access, public clinical staffing and service organization support a usual care pathway; dental/psychiatric waits, staffing and fiscal pressures remain constraints. Hospital product tariffs are not patient bills.",
      "assumption": "Public care is ordinarily affordable and clinically adequate for an eligible usual resident; 2025 regional access remains applicable to the urban FUA at cutoff. Unmeasured routine outcomes do not independently bar 60, but local charges and remaining waits must not amount to broad unmitigated necessary-care failure.",
      "conditionalAlternatives": [40, 80],
      "subpillars": {
        "access": "partial",
        "routine_quality": "unresolved",
        "specialist_capacity": "partial",
        "system_continuity": "partial"
